  <section|Exact source route and same-history
  binding><label|exact-source-route-and-same-history-binding>

  The inspected public route is <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG17/Joint.lean>. It destructures <verbatim|R.bought>,
  takes <verbatim|C := R.family>, builds <verbatim|Ribbons.Created C> from
  the run's stored history, and constructs <verbatim|Acme.Aroma C> on that
  same family as <verbatim|\<langle\>Ribbons.laurelE C ..., tabs,
  Ribbons.fugacious C ...\<rangle\>>. It subsequently calls
  <verbatim|Acme.readyA> on the received table/hierarchy and the current free
  comparison. <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.readyA> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Emanate.lean> calls
  <verbatim|produce_current>, obtains the actual conserved stress
  <verbatim|J.val>, and invokes <verbatim|shells_law ... J.val ... budget>.
  The output Ward laws are attached to the same returned first extension.
  This rules out substituting a stress from a nearby alternate constructor.

  <section|Exact producer crosswalk><label|exact-producer-crosswalk>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  step in the draft>>|<cell|<strong|Fully qualified
  declaration(s)>>|<cell|<strong|Path>>|<cell|<strong|Source content
  inspected>>>|<row|<cell|Uniform collar correction>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.ShellNode>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.sales>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.bricks>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/North/Brim.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Siroco.lean>>|<cell|For every fixed collar grid point,
  obtain a bounded grade-D label sequence and a late volume/period set. The
  late set may depend on the point; the coefficient and root-test bounds do
  not. At a fixed annulus scale only finitely many stencil points are used,
  so their late sets can be intersected before taking one compact subnet for
  the correction labels. <verbatim|sales> writes the correction as the
  two-component insertion minus the output label, invokes
  <verbatim|mutation>, and converts its quota through <verbatim|quota_stop>;
  <verbatim|bricks> supplies whole-collar geometry and late-filter
  choice.>>|<row|<cell|Price and scale economics>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pricey>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.lightness>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.laurelE>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fugacious>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.Economics>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/North/Burrough.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Economist.lean>>|<cell|With
  <verbatim|scale(i)=log(a_i^{-1})>, <verbatim|laurelE> chooses
  <verbatim|t=1+1/(64(d+12))> and a mesh subsequence satisfying
  <verbatim|scale(j_m)/scale(m)\<rightarrow\>t> (not
  <verbatim|a_{j_m}/a_m\<rightarrow\>t>). It combines <verbatim|pricey>,
  <verbatim|lightness>, opened Tabs, reference thresholds, and room to call
  <verbatim|bricks>; <verbatim|fees> is uniform in labels, grade relation,
  open level <verbatim|p_0> and level <verbatim|k>, and extraction order.
  <verbatim|fugacious> gives exponent <verbatim|-1> for
  <verbatim|fuga(i+1)>.>>|<row|<cell|Scale radius and two-channel payment
  definitions>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fuga>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pitts>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.ventola>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.mutation>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fundR>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.paid_new>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.paid_scale>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.stakes>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/North/Vert.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Burrough.lean>, <verbatim|North/Brick.lean>,
  <verbatim|North/Sultan.lean>, <verbatim|YM/MergeProof/Strudel.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|fuga(i)=128
  B_i^2 a_i> (so <verbatim|r_m=fuga(m+1)>);
  <verbatim|pitts(i)=exp(scale(i)/32)> and diverges because
  <verbatim|scale(i)\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>>; <verbatim|ventola> is the
  product of the two Boolean-channel picket budgets;
  <verbatim|stakes(p_0,k)=exp((a_{p_0}/a_k)^4 treasury_k+5)>. The two-channel
  construction consumes the local cost, run/throw, room, opened-count,
  chamber, root, and payment bounds. This is a source map, not a proof of
  these upstream producer estimates.>>|<row|<cell|Coefficient quota and
  root-test normalization>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.quota>,
  <verbatim|YM.Next.UVStress.quota_stop>,
  <verbatim|YM.Cells.Tiling.rootTest>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/Next/UV_STRESS/Least.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/Cells/Tiling.lean>>|<cell|The quota comparison gives a fixed
  factor from normalized terminal quota to coefficient norm; the root test is
  the normalized positive root of the finite Gibbs moment of the
  translated/reflected/conjugated cell product.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-stencil
  cancellation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.stencil_pay>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Stencil.lean>>|<cell|Approximate
  each rescaled insertion by a common grade-D tester with error bounded by
  the shell tolerance times a per-watch cost; sum against coefficients and
  use exact annihilation.>>|<row|<cell|Derivative
  chain>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.district>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.pelts>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.mountain>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.beneath>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Puppy.lean>,
  <verbatim|West/Peak.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Puppy.mountain> iterates the
  derivative-plan identity; <verbatim|Peak.beneath> gives the quantitative
  decay from <verbatim|Note.mills> when the raised tag plus two plus
  spectator-cloud degree is less than the scale exponent. The manuscript
  states the resulting separated-point majorant explicitly as an input,
  rather than claiming smoothness alone proves it. Its moving stress tag has
  degree 4; its cloud degree includes the fixed input insertion and
  spectators. In physical coordinates differentiation raises the tag without
  a scale factor; the factor <verbatim|a_{j_m}> appears on the lattice
  chord.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-node derivative
  interpolation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.angel>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.arctic>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.mitten>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.rink>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.reed>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Arch.lean>,
  <verbatim|West/Geo.lean>>|<cell|The manuscript derives the real recurrence
  <verbatim|A_0=1>, <verbatim|A_{q+1}=1+4P A_q> by pairing ordered nodes and
  applying the mean-value theorem, then handles complex values by
  real/imaginary parts. <verbatim|angel> supplies the same finite-stencil
  result; <verbatim|arctic> chooses nonzero lattice-coordinate nodes and
  <verbatim|mitten> keeps their segments in the collar.>>|<row|<cell|Collar
  to annulus interpolation>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.mars>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.arena>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.read_grid>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Fur.lean>,
  <verbatim|West/Stencil.lean>>|<cell|A nested induction over the axes not
  yet discretized chooses nonzero shifted grid nodes only at the final stage;
  the total displacement is at most <verbatim|4r/128=r/32>. The quantitative
  top derivative bound is <verbatim|C a_{j_m}^{q_*} r_m^{-(q_a+q_*+2+c_a)}>,
  whose logarithmic rate is negative by the displayed scale inequality. This
  transfers the grid bound to the annulus. <verbatim|arena> is the wider
  radius interval.>>|<row|<cell|Generic chamber and shrinking
  bump>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.cloudW>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.capB>, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.stretch_window>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.within_cap>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Fur.lean>,
  <verbatim|West/Blanca.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|cloudW> applies only when
  every coordinate is nonzero. A nested induction over the axes not yet
  discretized chooses nonzero shifted nodes only at the final stage;
  intermediate nodes need not be generic. The total displacement is at most
  <verbatim|4r/128=r/32>. The compactly supported bump is a valid window
  after shrinking below separation from other
  insertions.>>|<row|<cell|Annihilator-to-flux
  identity>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.zone>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.tenet>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Ozone.lean>,
  <verbatim|West/Blanca.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|zone> turns finite tester
  annihilation into uniform vanishing of the scaled insertion on the
  shrinking annulus. <verbatim|tenet> rescales the flux integral, sums
  finitely many components, and sends the fixed flux combination to
  zero.>>|<row|<cell|Finite-dimensional representation and
  extension>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.obtainable>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.annular_fieldA>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Bravo.lean>>|<cell|The
  annihilator criterion puts each finite flux vector in the range of the
  finite tester map. <verbatim|observes> gives a finite faithful watch set,
  which fixes one field for every additional watch; continuity and dense grid
  configurations extend the identity.>>|<row|<cell|Ward
  maps>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.map_shell>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.shells_law>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/West/Orange.lean>>|<cell|Flux
  is evaluated with the Killing field centered at the distinguished point,
  <verbatim|U(y-x_0)>. <verbatim|Bravo.raised> translates the configuration
  to a watch rooted at zero; <verbatim|moves_flux> and <verbatim|slide_disc>
  restore its center. Constant Killing fields give translation maps with
  <verbatim|D=d+1>; orbital skew fields give angular maps with
  <verbatim|D=d>. <verbatim|front_eval> identifies these maps with the flux
  rows. The angular map is complex-linear in the field and real-linear in the
  skew matrix.>>|<row|<cell|Public consequence>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Acme.readyA>,
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.extractible17>>|<cell|<verbatim|YM/MergeProof/Emanate.lean>,
  <verbatim|YM/RG17/Joint.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|readyA> calls
  <verbatim|shells_law> on the stress it has just produced; public
  selected-run extraction passes its same-family Aroma into this call.>>>>>

  <section|Proof correspondence and limitations><label|proof-correspondence-and-limitations>

  The numeric gates used in <verbatim|bricks> were read literally. Put
  <verbatim|lambda_i=scale(i)=log(a_i^{-1})>; the diverging exponential is in
  this logarithmic scale, not in the vanishing physical spacing. With
  <verbatim|Z_i=ventola(C.path.levels,j_i,i+1,\<delta\>,\<varphi\>,\<eta\>,\<delta\>_{i+1},A_i)>,
  <verbatim|X_i=exp(sqrt(hatBeta_{i+1}))>, <verbatim|e_i=32(1+columns_i)
  a_{i+1}^D X_i/Z_i>, and <verbatim|c_i=exp(lambda_i/32)>, <verbatim|pricey>
  supplies eventually <verbatim|Z_i\<gtr\>0>,
  <verbatim|march(c_i,\<eta\>,k,i)\<leq\>\<delta\>_i Z_i/(16 X_i)>, and
  <verbatim|32(1+columns_i)c_i \|\|alto(k,D)\|\|(e_i/gainChart(i,k))\<leq\>fly(D,k)/2>.
  Its logarithmic condition is <verbatim|((d+12)(1-t)\<gtr\>-1/32)>. \ At
  each fixed opened reference level <verbatim|p_0> and level <verbatim|k>,
  the remaining stake is <verbatim|exp((a_{p_0}/a_k)^4 treasury_k+5)>, hence
  constant as <verbatim|i\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>> while
  <verbatim|c_i\<rightarrow\>\<infty\>>. The separate <verbatim|lightness>
  output is eventually <verbatim|32 fuga(i+1)\<leq\>a_{p_0}> and
  <verbatim|a_{i+1}(B_{i+1}^2+1+2*1024*B_{i+1}^2)\<leq\>a_{p_0}>.
  <verbatim|bricks> uses the first gate for collar room and the second to fit
  the finite stencil into the coarse chamber. \ This exact arithmetic is in
  the manuscript; it is not a proof of the sublemmas feeding these receipts.

  The manuscript gives the measure-theoretic shrinking argument explicitly,
  conditional on the shell-node input and the displayed separated-point
  majorants from <verbatim|Peak.beneath>. At each fixed stencil point the
  bounded counterterm sequence is extracted once in the common fused filter,
  using finite-dimensional compactness; that one limit is used for every
  watch in the finite family. The cost-limit identities then approximate all
  tester values on the same filter refinement, so their weighted sum cancels.
  No watch-dependent subsequences are used.

  For the bump with unit-scale profile <verbatim|capB>, the source support of
  its derivative lies between radii <verbatim|1/2> and <verbatim|1>; after
  dilation by <verbatim|r_m>, it lies inside the source annulus
  <verbatim|r_m/4\<less\>\|x\|\<less\>2r_m>. The four-dimensional Jacobian,
  one derivative of the bump, and homogeneity degree <verbatim|p> give the
  factor <verbatim|r_m^(3+p)>. The grade relation in the two source
  propositions implies <verbatim|h=3+p>, so the shell estimate has exactly
  the required scaling. The componentwise integral has an integrable
  compactly supported weight; uniform annulus decay therefore makes it tend
  to zero. Conservation/window-change identifies it with a fixed flux
  combination. This proves the exact annihilator statement, not merely
  asymptotic flux decay.

  The finite-dimensional range argument is expanded in ordinary linear
  algebra: every functional annihilating the tester range also annihilates
  the flux vector, hence the flux vector belongs to that range. The finite
  faithful tester set ensures that the representative is independent of the
  added watch. The continuity extension is the source's
  <verbatim|frequently_eq> argument using grid density and continuous
  flux/disc maps.

  The shell economics are recorded at the level of their actual output and
  composition. The manuscript does not prove the shell-node output from those
  inputs. In particular, it does not rederive the primitive analytic
  estimates feeding <verbatim|pricey>, <verbatim|lightness>, the paid
  local-cost receipt, the cofinal run/throw receipt, or the two-channel
  construction. In particular, <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.pricey>
  imports <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.quilled>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.mintN>,
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.fuchsia>, and
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Ribbons.seeing>; <verbatim|lightness> imports
  <verbatim|fuchsia> and <verbatim|briar>. The proof of the paid local-cost
  and run/throw records is not rederived here. Those are genuine upstream
  quantitative proof obligations if the monograph is to discharge the whole
  source chain here. This draft does not claim their names prove the
  estimates. The listed declarations were read, but their transitive producer
  proofs were not exhaustively expanded in this bounded unit. The annular
  annihilator, finite-dimensional range argument, and root-centered
  translation/rotation conversion are proved conditional on the explicit
  shell-node statement; the public endpoint chain is a correspondence, not a
  completed proof that this statement is available.

  <section|Literature search><label|literature-search>

  The shared <verbatim|blueprint/background/> contains only the
  SU(2)-simplicity note and the directory instructions; no accepted
  Ward/stress-annulus result applies to this finite-volume insertion and its
  project-specific scale budgets. The local bibliography likewise has no
  Ward/stress entry. Accordingly, this unit invokes no external theorem: the
  compactly supported rescaling, finite annihilator linear algebra, and
  four-coordinate interpolation are proved directly. No new literature
  citation is substituted for the shell estimates.

